Root cause:
The bug was caused by the introduction of a mechanism to batch packets for devmap that led to calling `xdp_do_flush()` in a process context. This approach resulted in potential missed flushes on different processors because simply disabling preemption was not effective, as the process could migrate across processors. The patch reverted the changes that added this functionality, as it could lead to unreliable behavior in handling XDP (eXpress Data Path) flushing.
